      "text_raw": "If the compliance voltage of\n0.4 V is still too high, one\nsingle output transistor can\nbe used.\nAn opamp is then used to\nprovide feedback around\nthe input device M1. Its\ndrain voltage is then only\n0.2 V, which is a lot less than\nthe 0.9 V in a conventional\ncurrent mirror (for a V of\nT\n0.7 V).\nThe output impedance is\nnot very high. It is simply\nthe output resistance of the\noutput transistor M2.\nThere are better uses for\nan opamp as shown next.",
      "text": "If the compliance voltage of 0.4 V is still too high, one single output transistor can be used. An opamp is then used to provide feedback around the input device M1. Its drain voltage is then only 0.2 V, which is a lot less than the 0.9 V in a conventional current mirror (for a V of T 0.7 V). The output impedance is not very high. It is simply the output resistance of the output transistor M2. There are better uses for an opamp as shown next."
